{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And HaShem said.</b> It is difficult in light of what we have established above, that the language of saying (amirah) denotes matters that gladden the heart and announces greatness and honor — yet here He shows me that He said nothing but the tidings of an evil decree. It may be explained according to what they said in the midrash (Numbers Rabbah 19:12), that Moshe said before HaShem: Behold, You have decreed upon me to die in the wilderness with this wicked generation, etc.; the generations will say that I am equal to them — let it be written concerning me for what I was punished! Therefore it is written <b>ye'an lo he'emantem bi</b> (because you did not believe in Me), etc. — end quote. And this is what HaShem intimated by saying <b>vayomer</b> — a language of exaltation for Moshe and Aharon, for He wrote their sin on account of which they died, which is ״יַעַן לֹא״ (because you did not), etc., so that the generations would not consider them equal to the wicked generation, heaven forbid."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:11:14.297434904Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}